cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build upon Legal-Mamba, please cite this repository."

title: "Legal-Mamba: A Domain-Specific Mamba Language Model for Indian Criminal Law"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Chanana"
    given-names: "Naman"

abstract: >-
  Legal-Mamba is a compact autoregressive language model based on the
  Mamba State Space Model architecture and trained on a curated corpus
  of Indian criminal-law text. The repository includes corpus preparation,
  a custom BPE tokenizer, model implementation, training pipeline,
  checkpoint metadata, training history, and legal-text generation examples.

repository-code: "https://github.com/Rishy-09/legal-mamba-indian-criminal-law"
url: "https://github.com/Rishy-09/legal-mamba-indian-criminal-law"

license: Apache-2.0

keywords:
  - mamba
  - state-space-model
  - language-model
  - legal-nlp
  - legal-ai
  - indian-law
  - pytorch
  - natural-language-processing